 ## Overview
-Sketch-based Cloud Volume Retrieval via SVD is a method for retrieving realistic 3D cloud volumes from a pre-simulated database by matching a user-sketched 2D shape to 3D data using Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) basis vectors for efficient similarity calculation [S1]. It differs from direct voxel comparison by projecting both the query and database volumes into a low-dimensional subspace, reducing the computational cost of similarity search from proportional to the total number of voxels $M$ to proportional to the number of basis vectors $K$ [S1]. This method builds on [Query Shape Generation from Vertical Sketch](13408-query-shape-generation-from-vertical-sketch.md) by converting the generated query shape into a volumetric representation suitable for database matching.
+Sketch-based Cloud Volume Retrieval via SVD is a method for retrieving realistic 3D cloud volumes from a pre-simulated database by matching a user-sketched 2D shape to 3D data using Singular Value Decomposition (SVD) basis vectors for efficient similarity calculation [S1]. It differs from direct voxel comparison by projecting both the query and database volumes into a low-dimensional subspace, reducing the computational cost of similarity search from proportional to the total number of voxels $M$ to proportional to the number of basis vectors $K$ [S1]. The method converts the generated query shape into a volumetric representation suitable for database matching by creating a bounding box and subdividing it into a uniform grid [S1].
 
